WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.670
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.930
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.800
This episode features a story about Yaya and Rima!

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.990
They get lost beneath the school.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.710
We have to save them!

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.340
This is a job for...

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.150
Pepe-tan and...

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.150
Kusukusu!

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.280
We can handle this ourselves-dechu.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.490
Ready, set...

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:22.910
Bala-Balance!

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.960
Uh...

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:42.180
If you were to walk so the wind fluttered the edge of your cape,

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:48.570
people would look up at you in quiet admiration.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:55.870
You can say spicy things like "it's not my style," if you want,

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:02.290
but I know who you really are because I'm your friend!

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.160
Stand! Bow!

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.690
Nice and orderly now!

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:09.530
And once that's done,

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:14.800
it's time to start the school day.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:22.420
I like Mondays because I can see all my friends.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:28.820
There's nothing wrong with being abnormally happy.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:35.990
At lunch break, we have tea in the Royal Garden,

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:43.330
where I tell you all my secrets!

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:08.900
Now look here, Kiseki-san! I don't see you cleaning!

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.760
Do you seriously expect the King to clean?

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.170
It might be best to just do as she says right now...

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:17.130
You don't want to make her angry, right?

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:17.700
Hmph!

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:23.460
The King should be of service to his people, should he not?

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.000
Hey, Tadase-kun...

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.960
The other day, did you notice the sound from the tuning fork suddenly stopped?

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.310
Yes, it seemed to.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:38.670
It's like they stopped it on purpose.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:40.730
I wonder why they'd do that.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.100
Thank you.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:46.400
What's Easter's true goal?

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.990
Why, hello! Having a little cleaning party?

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:51.270
How commendable.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:57.130
Didn't you say that today is Clean the School Day?

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.450
And on the spur of the moment this morning, too.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.780
Oh yeah, I did say that, didn't I? Sorry.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.450
All right, then. Do a bang-up job, okay?

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.190
Get cleaning, now.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.200
Huh?

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:16.130
Where'd the Chairman go?

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.990
He vanished!

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.400
Maybe he has access to a secret passageway or something.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.640
Enough about that! Back to cleaning!

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.380
There is no time for idle chit-chat!

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.680
Yes, boss...

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.810
Episode 95
Rima, Yaya, and the Pearls that Bind Them!

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:37.070
Cleaning is so fun! Cleaning is so fun!

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:40.930
Cleaning is so fun! Cleaning is so fun!

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:44.200
Cleaning is so fun! Cleaning is so...

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.030
Yaya!

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.830
Yaya, you're not doing it right.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.480
Uh-huh, whatever.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.840
Rima-tan sure can be picky.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.280
You can say that again-dechu.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.710
Yaya...

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:00.950
C-C-Cleaning is so fun!

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:14.900
I'm sick of this! Cleaning is so annoying!

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.990
No more! No more! No more!

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:21.360
Huh?

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.490
What the heck is this?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:41.100
We've discovered a secret passage!

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.760
I've always suspected this school was a bit different, but I never expected <i>this</i>.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.240
Maybe there's a secret underground base-dechu.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.500
Let's explore-dechu!

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:49.890
Yeah!

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:50.890
Kusukusu!

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.250
Let's go check it out, too!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.350
It'll be fine, don't worry! And we're off!

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.540
What a perfect atmosphere for exploration.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:12.840
Yaya...

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.610
It'll be fine! No worries!

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.250
Isn't exploring a secret base a super fun idea?

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:22.340
How does this open-dechu?

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.220
Let's go, Rima-tan!

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.610
Yaya...

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.430
Amazing!

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.440
This is really some fine work-dechu.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:48.110
I could have sworn this was the area Rima-chan and Yaya-chan were handling...

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:52.400
Yaya, I think we should head back.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.420
This atmosphere is perfect!

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.660
Right or left?

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.280
Which way do you think we should go?

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.150
I don't know and I don't care! I'm going back!

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.490
Rima!

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:11.010
Let's go just a bit farther-dechu.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.030
Three against one! You lose, Rima-tan!

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:15.330
Let's go!

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:15.830
Go!

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:16.920
Yeah!

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.570
Yuiki-san and Mashiro-san are gone?

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:29.780
Yes, although they left their brooms and supplies.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.530
I bet Yaya's just slacking and fooling around somewhere!

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:36.620
But Mashiro-san is missing, too.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.980
That's true... Where do you think they went?

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:06.860
There's nothing in here.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.320
Looks like a dead end.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:16.290
Maybe we should head back now.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.930
Oopsie.. I think we're trapped.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:31.410
R-Rima!

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:33.890
Rima-tan?

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.340
Just leave her locked in here.

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:41.850
She'll fetch a pretty ransom!

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.900
You can blame your parents for this.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.900
No...

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.180
No... Help me!

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:54.210
Rima-tan?

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.080
What's wrong?

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.890
Are you okay-dechu?

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.100
What should I do?

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:02.870
I think she's reliving the time she was nearly kidnapped!

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:03.990
Rima-tan?

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.710
Let me go!

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.390
Let me out of here...

00:08:07.390 --> 00:08:09.660
Rima? Rima!

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:12.800
It's okay-dechu. It's just a bad dream-dechu...

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.930
No... No...

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:16.460
Stop it, stop it!

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.790
If you get scared, I'll end up freaking out, too!

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:21.880
Cut it out!

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:27.860
Yaya?

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.260
Can I see a smile?

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.950
That way, I won't be scared.

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:40.200
Yaya! Rima!

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:43.850
Where did those two go?

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.850
Kusukusu and Pepe aren't here either.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:48.630
How dare those commoners worry their King so!

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:50.700
Let's split up and search for them.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:52.630
Amu-chan, you look out by the fields.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.560
Hotori-kun, check behind the school.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:55.510
Right.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:02.750
Do you remember what I told you?

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:05.760
One time, I was almost kidnapped.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.350
They didn't manage to pull it off, though.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.100
They didn't?

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:10.820
No.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:14.480
They locked her up, but she was quickly rescued.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:20.500
But after that happened, my mom and dad...

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:23.040
This is your fault!

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.670
You're always like this! You blame every bad thing on me!

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:30.700
And you leave me to handle everything for Rima!

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.840
Because I thought I could trust you!

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:34.580
Trust?

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.020
You're just dumping her on me!

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:37.260
What did you say?!

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:52.600
What was that for?

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:57.860
It's how I deal when I'm thinking weird thoughts or remembering bad things.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.140
So it happens to you sometimes, too?

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:01.470
What kind of heartless monster do you take me for?

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:04.250
I'm a delicate lady at heart, you know!

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.370
Even I feel down at times.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:09.970
You should try it, Rima-tan.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.500
Now, stand up!

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:16.120
Scream your heart out!

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:18.430
Like, "Uwah!"

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:21.340
Louder!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.690
Louder, louder!

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:27.980
Blast all those bad things right out of your heart!

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:06.040
Feel better?

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.450
A little.

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:08.730
Oh yeah...

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:13.310
I saw something on TV a while back. Do you know how pearls are made?

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:18.910
You place a small piece of something like plastic inside an oyster,

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.930
and then that becomes the nucleus of a pearl, right?

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.140
Right.

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:26.130
But it got me thinking.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:30.410
Wouldn't that be really painful for the oyster?

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:33.670
I mean, it basically gets something stuck in its belly.

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:40.390
It can't take it out, and the more it moves, the more it hurts...

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:41.930
But you know...

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:49.080
That's why, after a super long time and lots of tears, it makes a pearl.

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:53.570
And maybe that's why pearls are so beautiful.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:58.120
So, after thinking about it that way, I realized something.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:03.420
Even if someone hurts it, the oyster turns all its pain into a pearl.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.240
You think so?

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.540
Yeah!

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:14.460
Yaya-tan, I think we can get out through here-dechu!

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:21.000
Are you okay?

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.550
Yep, we're fine!

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:24.810
Okay, we'll get help-dechu!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:31.000
We're countin' on you guys!

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.690
Where could they have gone?

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:39.510
When you can't find something you're looking for...

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:40.890
It's time to use this!

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:42.060
No, this!

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:44.660
Nuh-uh! This works best!

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.770
Great luck!

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:50.770
It says you'll be lucky in love!

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:54.160
Excellent finances! Your allowance might go up!

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:56.490
What are you guys doing?

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:59.850
We're wishing for the missing people to appear!

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:01.620
Oh really now?

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:03.300
Amu-chan!

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.210
Any luck?

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:05.130
No...

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.800
Could they have left the school grounds?

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.660
Honestly, where are they?

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:24.890
Madame Nobuko!

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:26.850
Been a while, hasn't it?

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:33.040
I am the charismatic Guardian Spirit Fortune-Teller that happens to be passing by, Saeki Nobuko!

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:42.140
Madame Saeki, what are you doing?

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:45.430
Like I said, just passing by.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:47.890
Wait, aren't you...

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:49.660
I could have sworn...

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.240
U-Um...

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:55.500
This is her twin brother!

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:59.750
That's right, I am Fujisaki Nagihiko! Pleased to meet you!

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:07.490
Oh! Would you help us, Madame?

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:09.500
What is she talking about?

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:12.000
Some friends of ours went missing.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.080
With your fortune-telling, we'll find them in a jiffy!

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:20.180
Pretty please, Madame Saeki?

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:24.050
This lovely boy... This lovely boy is...

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:29.780
I-I suppose someone has to do it.

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:31.450
All right!

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:39.440
Imprisoned light.

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:43.370
A world none would venture to.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:46.160
And? And?

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:48.490
A-And?

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.700
Madame Saeki!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.490
Madame!

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.150
What are you doing?

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:55.830
The taping is about to begin!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.690
O-Oh, that's true, isn't it?

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.120
Well then, until next time!

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.520
What was she doing here?

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:10.050
She said she was just passing by, but...

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:15.260
What did she mean by "imprisoned light?"

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:18.220
A place light can't reach, maybe?

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:20.740
Perhaps they're trapped somewhere?

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:23.810
What about the world no one would go to?

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.230
Maybe it's a place that nobody uses.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:43.760
We have to hurry, or Yaya-tan will get worried!

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.250
Why?

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:49.720
She puts on a brave face, but Yaya-tan actually hates being alone-dechu.

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:54.320
I hope Pepe-chan finds help soon.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:56.510
I'm sure she will.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:09.870
Did you find them?

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:11.700
No...

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:13.580
What are we going to do?

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:16.560
Is there any other place that no one normally uses?

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:17.660
Don't worry.

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:20.160
We'll find them.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:21.950
Yeah!

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:27.670
Pepe-chan and Kusukusu still aren't back...

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.760
Yaya, what's the matter?

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:33.260
You were cheering me up before...

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:37.100
To be honest, I'm really just a big baby at heart...

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.370
Can I stay like this?

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:44.850
Sure.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.190
What's the matter?

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:58.160
We passed by this place before, didn't we?

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:01.480
There's a chance...

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:04.240
...that we're lost-dechu.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:28.940
Rima-tan you smell nice; just like my mom.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:40.150
It was a fall day, just before winter.

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:44.720
The sky was filled with dark, gray clouds, and a cold wind was blowing.

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:48.630
A lone fox was walking in the mountains,

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:53.880
when a freezing rain suddenly began to fall.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:58.680
Scared, the fox sought shelter in a nearby cave.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:03.100
"Lucky me, it thought, as it peered inside.

00:18:05.340 --> 00:18:08.670
But in that cave, it discovered a huge bear.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:12.120
The fox shook from terror.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:13.670
Then the bear said:

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:15.310
"Hey, fox,"

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:17.860
all of a sudden.

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:20.490
"Um, yes? What is it?"

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:25.140
"Your tail looks soft and fluffy and warm."

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:27.740
"Let me use it as a scarf."

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:29.250
"Uh, sure..."

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:37.910
So the fox wrapped his tail around the bear's neck, just like a scarf.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.430
But then...

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:42.960
"I'm still cold. Can I hold you?"

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:46.880
asked the bear as he pressed the fox tightly to him.

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.560
The fox thought he was as good as done for.

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:54.620
But as time passed...

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:59.750
They both slowly got warmer and warmer.

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:02.570
Outside, a chill autumn rain was falling,

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:06.530
but the two of them were warm and cozy.

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:10.020
Warm and cozy...

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.460
I really loved that story as a child.

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:19.520
I wonder why?

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:23.430
Maybe because my mom and dad read it to me.

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:32.000
Pepe!

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.780
Kusukusu!

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.990
Just where are they?

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:37.440
Over here!

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.890
Over where?

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:43.590
We can finally see the sky!

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:46.490
Pepe! Kusukusu!

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:56.020
Why would this be here?

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:57.630
Hurry-dechu!

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:03.380
They're behind this door-dechu!

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.950
Rima!

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:08.210
Yaya-chan!

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:11.330
It's no use, it won't open!

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:12.840
Let's ask a teacher for help!

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:13.980
Wait.

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:15.980
Perhaps...

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:28.600
Yaya! Rima!

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:35.410
Amu-chi? Good morning...

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:36.900
Took you long enough.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:40.660
Rima!

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:41.580
Yaya-tan!

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:43.600
Thank goodness!

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:53.770
Man, I didn't know what was gonna happen to us!

00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:57.790
You had us totally worried.

00:20:57.790 --> 00:20:59.510
You, too, Rima!

00:20:59.510 --> 00:21:01.150
I'm sorry, Amu.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:03.890
All that matters is that we found you.

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:05.410
Exactly.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.610
All's well that ends well.

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:13.460
It seems the underground room I built quite inconvenienced you.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:15.420
You made that room?

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:18.880
I should've known.

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:22.460
Well, here's my way of saying sorry.

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:24.500
Cake!

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:25.630
When did he have time to bake?

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:27.410
Delicious!

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:28.200
It really is!

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:31.360
It's unbelievably soft and sweet!

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:35.860
About that oyster you told me about...

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:41.290
I think that even if they have a pearl inside, they'll never realize how pretty it is.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:44.280
Somebody else has to discover it.

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:49.070
But why an underground room?

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:50.920
Isn't it fun?

00:21:50.920 --> 00:21:52.080
Fun, he says?

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:56.710
Honestly...

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:12.670
Warm and cozy, right?

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:16.260
Yeah, warm and cozy.

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:33.220
You sure do seem determined.

00:22:34.630 --> 00:22:39.270
So even if you screw up, it'll somehow turn out all right.

00:22:39.970 --> 00:22:46.640
How about you just trust in yourself?

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:53.100
Take that first step and everything will work out fine.

00:22:53.710 --> 00:23:00.030
Even if people see through your cool exterior, keep marching on.

00:23:00.450 --> 00:23:09.110
Look up at the blue sky and everything will reset!

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:12.750
Take it easy! Take it easy!

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:23.290
Try to relax those shoulders and clear your mind.

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:30.000
The more you do it, the easier it'll get, so keep taking it easy.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:35.200
Ride the flow of time and you'll be...

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:39.000
Shining! Shining! Shining!

00:23:50.390 --> 00:23:53.540
Finally! Finally! We finally know where Ikuto is!

00:23:53.540 --> 00:23:57.050
And now Yoru can finally see him again, right?

00:23:57.050 --> 00:24:01.000
But we can't be too happy yet. He's still being controlled.

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:03.520
Looks like Easter's up to something, as usual.

00:24:03.520 --> 00:24:07.160
I bet there'll be trouble at the classical music concert!

00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:10.010
Amu-chan, please be careful!

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:12.190
Next time on Shugo Chara!! Doki:

00:24:12.190 --> 00:24:14.890
Unheard Pleas, Shattered Feelings!

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:17.620
Have you really forgotten everything?

00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:19.620
Talk to me, Ikuto!
